{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyQTtAbrwdJZeg3BGsk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FUsCAGspYkBJVixshPCPYq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/opwolf-plan-research-OCq3d6/hub/lib/hub/examples && grep -n \"AIHub\\.\\|<meta name=\\\"hub\" arena.html | head -60 && echo ===== && grep -n \"^\\s*//\" arena.html | head -60","description":"Scan the shared-world arena example for hub API usage"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4630,"cache_read_input_tokens":109899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4630},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825","uuid":"6d521f25-64be-4c6d-88e2-0afb916d8d76","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:47.465Z","request_id":"req_011CggyQTeHJUyvKuW8HqDuD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FUsCAGspYkBJVixshPCPYq":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/opwolf-plan-research-OCq3d6/hub/lib/hub/examples && grep -n \"AIHub\\.\\|<meta name=\\\"hub\" arena.html | head -60 && echo ===== && grep -n \"^\\s*//\" arena.html | head -60","description":"Scan the shared-world arena example for hub API usage"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUsCAGspYkBJVixshPCPYq","type":"tool_result","content":"9:<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n10:<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n11:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n12:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n13:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n14:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n15:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n16:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n526:// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n666:let lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\n670:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n673:  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n680:  AIHub.ready();\n681:  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n682:  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n688:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n693:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n694:  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n716:  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n725:    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n748:  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n757:  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n786:  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n805:      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n811:    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n812:    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n846:  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n848:    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n=====\n123:  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n124:  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n125:  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n136:  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n137:  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n145:  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n146:  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n147:  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n148:  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n256:      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n297:      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n516:// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n517:// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n518:// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n519:// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n520://   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n521://   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n522://   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n523://   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n524:// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n525:// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n526:// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n527:// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n528:// First to TARGET stars wins.\n555:// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n556:// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n557:// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\n564:  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n575:// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n576:// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\n624:// ---- state shared by both modes\n653:// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\n661:// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n662:// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n663:// is drawn where you put it.\n677:  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n778:// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\n803:      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825","uuid":"6e2dbf87-b039-4351-88e2-d7a0be1aabd2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:47.489Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"9:<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n10:<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n11:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n12:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n13:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n14:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n15:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n16:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n526:// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n666:let lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\n670:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n673:  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n680:  AIHub.ready();\n681:  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n682:  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n688:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n693:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n694:  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n716:  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n725:    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n748:  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n757:  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n786:  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n805:      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n811:    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n812:    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n846:  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n848:    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n=====\n123:  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n124:  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n125:  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n136:  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n137:  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n145:  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n146:  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n147:  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n148:  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n256:      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n297:      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n516:// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n517:// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n518:// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n519:// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n520://   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n521://   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n522://   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n523://   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n524:// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n525:// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n526:// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n527:// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n528:// First to TARGET stars wins.\n555:// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n556:// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n557:// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\n564:  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n575:// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n576:// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\n624:// ---- state shared by both modes\n653:// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\n661:// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n662:// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n663:// is drawn where you put it.\n677:  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n778:// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\n803:      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.","stderr":"\n