{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AoRJQroA5AnaDdXHG191Eo","type":"tool_result","content":"448:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n540:**Random Mode**. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n571:  the browser, as `localStorage['ai-hub:relay-only']`).\n572:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n682:own, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\n689:an override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n705:checks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n706:(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.\n186:Capture and inspect a real screenshot strip at `covers/<slug>/0.jpg`, `1.jpg`\n189:do not count as screenshots; keep uncertain model details unset.\n196:in the Couch, with its own screenshots and URL for comparison. Its genre and\n457:(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\n502:awk 'NR % 7 == 0' .cache/wave1.txt > .cache/pilot.txt        # a pilot of about thirty, small to large\n531:one. Run a pilot of about thirty varied games, read the pass rate and cost per\n533:for you: commit what passed in batches of about fifty.\n553:about half a minute from one game to the next, less when everyone is ready\n636:  works as before. The free project pauses after about a week without use;\n654:**Real screenshots** — `pnpm shots` opens each game, waits for its title screen\n778:  shots.mjs       optional screenshots\n813:library shelf cut to the files games actually load (about 14,700 files in all,\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825","uuid":"5b3140c4-2a80-411e-a511-904c560d6987","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:51.172Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"448:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n540:**Random Mode**. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n571:  the browser, as `localStorage['ai-hub:relay-only']`).\n572:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n682:own, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\n689:an override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n705:checks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n706:(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.\n186:Capture and inspect a real screenshot strip at `covers/<slug>/0.jpg`, `1.jpg`\n189:do not count as screenshots; keep uncertain model details unset.\n196:in the Couch, with its own screenshots and URL for comparison. Its genre and\n457:(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\n502:awk 'NR % 7 == 0' .cache/wave1.txt > .cache/pilot.txt        # a pilot of about thirty, small to large\n531:one. Run a pilot of about thirty varied games, read the pass rate and cost per\n533:for you: commit what passed in batches of about fifty.\n553:about half a minute from one game to the next, less when everyone is ready\n636:  works as before. The free project pauses after about a week without use;\n654:**Real screenshots** — `pnpm shots` opens each game, waits for its title screen\n778:  shots.mjs       optional screenshots\n813:library shelf cut to the files games actually load (about 14,700 files in all,","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AoRJQroA5AnaDdXHG191Eo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyR2aSW61GshoTwapC4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MEF83YGcJwQSw3Y8MZ8c9f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/opwolf-plan-research-OCq3d6/hub && sed -n 670,720p README.md","description":"Read the AI Hub README section on game metadata tags"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":919,"cache_read_input_tokens":116743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":919},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825","uuid":"7cb90f4e-cee0-459c-8e1e-882350caaf1e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:53.326Z","request_id":"req_011CggyR2Mo4B5VAY41nYuYe","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MEF83YGcJwQSw3Y8MZ8c9f":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/opwolf-plan-research-OCq3d6/hub && sed -n 670,720p README.md","description":"Read the AI Hub README section on game metadata tags"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MEF83YGcJwQSw3Y8MZ8c9f","type":"tool_result","content":"    \"model\": \"Claude Opus 5\",\n    \"harness\": \"Claude Code\",\n    \"status\": \"polished\",\n    \"tags\": [\"pixel-art\", \"dungeon\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nHere is the part worth knowing: **the filter rails are not declared anywhere.**\nThey are read off whatever the games actually carry. Fill in `model` on a few\ngames and a Model rail appears on the wall by itself; remove them and it goes.\nAny field works, including ones invented on the spot. A game can also carry its\nown, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\nvalues are nearly all different (a build id, a URL) is searchable but never\nbecomes a rail. Every field is searchable. `harness` is searched and shown in\nthe drawer but never gets a rail, and neither do `source` and `series`, which\nhave Original, Inspired and the stacks.\n\n`collection` comes from the folder a game sits in, but it is an ordinary field:\nan override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n\nThe library's own catalogue uses these fields, all in `data/overrides.json`:\n\n| Field | What it is | On the wall |\n|---|---|---|\n| `genre` | one of a fixed list (Racing, Platformer, Life Sim, Tech Demo…) | the Genre rail, and the cabinet's panel |\n| `type` | `Game`, `Tech demo` or `Tool` | the shelf: games, or tech demos & tools |\n| `tags` | 2–5 from a fixed vocabulary (`3d`, `retro`, `co-op`, `touch`…) | the Tags rail |\n| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n| `source` | the classic a game riffs on, as it is titled (`Dragon Quest IX`); none for an original | Original or Inspired, the stacks, the drawer, and search |\n| `series` | the franchise, only when it is not the source itself (`Dragon Quest` for `Dragon Quest IX`) | the stacks |\n| `controls` | a one-line summary | the drawer |\n| `description` | one or two plain sentences | the drawer |\n\nEvery game with the same `source` must have the same `series`; `pnpm test`\nchecks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.\nGenre, Collection, Type and Players follow it when they exist; the\nrest follow by how many games carry them. `docs/curation-2026-09-24.md`\nrecords how the library was curated: which file of each game was kept, and\nwhich older iterations it replaced. `docs/curation-2026-09-28.md` records the\nimport from the source-named GPT-games folder and maps the old slugs to the\ncurrent ones; `docs/curation-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md` records the smaller\nimport that followed it.\n\nSetting `\"hidden\": true` drops a game from the catalogue entirely.\n`\"restricted\": true` keeps it in the catalogue but off the wall, where only dev\nsettings can bring it back — used for the companionship-business sims.\n\n### Dev settings\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825","uuid":"cbe64715-9c12-491d-9385-95065e39129b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:53.341Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    \"model\": \"Claude Opus 5\",\n    \"harness\": \"Claude Code\",\n    \"status\": \"polished\",\n    \"tags\": [\"pixel-art\", \"dungeon\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nHere is the part worth knowing: **the filter rails are not declared anywhere.**\nThey are read off whatever the games actually carry. Fill in `model` on a few\ngames and a Model rail appears on the wall by itself; remove them and it goes.\nAny field works, including ones invented on the spot. A game can also carry its\nown, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\nvalues are nearly all different (a build id, a URL) is searchable but never\nbecomes a rail. Every field is searchable. `harness` is searched and shown in\nthe drawer but never gets a rail, and neither do `source` and `series`, which\nhave Original, Inspired and the stacks.\n\n`collection` comes from the folder a game sits in, but it is an ordinary field:\nan override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n\nThe library's own catalogue uses these fields, all in `data/overrides.json`:\n\n| Field | What it is | On the wall |\n|---|---|---|\n| `genre` | one of a fixed list (Racing, Platformer, Life Sim, Tech Demo…) | the Genre rail, and the cabinet's panel |\n| `type` | `Game`, `Tech demo` or `Tool` | the shelf: games, or tech demos & tools |\n| `tags` | 2–5 from a fixed vocabulary (`3d`, `retro`, `co-op`, `touch`…) | the Tags rail |\n| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n| `source` | the classic a game riffs on, as it is titled (`Dragon Quest IX`); none for an original | Original or Inspired, the stacks, the drawer, and search |\n| `series` | the franchise, only when it is not the source itself (`Dragon Quest` for `Dragon Quest IX`) | the stacks |\n| `controls` | a one-line summary | the drawer |\n| `description` | one or two plain sentences | the drawer |\n\nEvery game with the same `source` must have the same `series`; `pnpm test`\nchecks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.\nGenre, Collection, Type and Players follow it when they exist; the\nrest follow by how many games carry them. `docs/curation-2026-09-24.md`\nrecords how the library was curated: which file of each game was kept, and\nwhich older iterations it replaced. `docs