{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyTxLGxGj3nhmN34faN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PCZuYGXpRQfq6yLHqMoSQ3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/micha/.cache/opwolf-plan-research-OCq3d6/engine/dist/handoff; cd $H && sed -n 560,580p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-700; grep -n \"glyphs\\b\\|'glyphs'\\|key: 'glyphs'\\|symbols\" my-3d2dge.js | head -12","description":"Read the settings API and how button symbols are set"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3548,"cache_read_input_tokens":138421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3548},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825","uuid":"f2027302-9259-41e4-884b-bdf635e0337b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:38.238Z","request_id":"req_011CggyTwzgs9ieVFwLejMZV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PCZuYGXpRQfq6yLHqMoSQ3":{"command":"H=/home/micha/.cache/opwolf-plan-research-OCq3d6/engine/dist/handoff; cd $H && sed -n 560,580p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-700; grep -n \"glyphs\\b\\|'glyphs'\\|key: 'glyphs'\\|symbols\" my-3d2dge.js | head -12","description":"Read the settings API and how button symbols are set"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PCZuYGXpRQfq6yLHqMoSQ3","type":"tool_result","content":"- `E.showError(title, e)`: show an error in the red box at the top of the page (the engine does it for errors in update and draw); a click hides it. Before play has started it shows on the boot screen instead, as a report a player can screenshot\n\n## 10b. Standard features\n\n- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n- `fullscreen.enter(quiet)`: go full screen. Browsers allow it only from a tap, click or key press: call it from one (a button, the menu, a key's update step). Returns a promise of whether it worked (a refusal is kept in failed and noted on screen, unless quiet)\n- `fullscreen.exit()`: leave full screen (Escape and the phone's back gesture do it too)\n- `fullscreen.on`: true while the page is full screen\n- `fullscreen.standalone`: true when the page was opened from a home screen as an app (no browser bars: nothing to go full screen from)\n- `fullscreen.supported`: true where this page can go full screen (not an iPhone, which has Add to Home Screen instead; not a frame without permission; not headless)\n- `fullscreen.toggle()`: full screen on or off, as the player asked (the corner's button, the menu): their choice is kept in settings.fullscreen, so a game starting on a phone goes full screen by itself only while they haven't turned it off\n- `fullscreen.failed = null`: game: the game it serves; failed: why the last request was refused (a message), or null\n\n## 10c. Boot\n\n789:    /** glyphs: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' |\n792:    this.glyphs = 'auto'; this.rumbleScale = .6; this.padLost = false;\n895:   *  button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family) */\n904:  /** the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says */\n906:    if (this.glyphs && this.glyphs !== 'auto') return this.glyphs;\n1302: * 6. PIXEL FONT  3x5 glyphs for in-world numbers and labels\n1354:  normal: { glyphs: parseFont(G57), h: 7, desc: 2, gap: 1, space: 3, upper: false },\n1355:  tiny: { glyphs: parseFont(GLYPHS), h: 5, desc: 0, gap: 2, space: 3, upper: true, mono: 3 }\n1369:  _glyph(f, ch) { return f.glyphs[f.upper ? ch.toUpperCase() : ch] || f.glyphs[ch.toUpperCase()] || f.glyphs['?']; },\n1426:   * Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge.\n2999:  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { g.input.glyphs = v; } },\n9107: *    changes; the controller's dead zone, aim, symbols and vibration; the touch buttons' side, size and opacity; restore\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825","uuid":"a06e2fee-7c93-420a-bf04-20ae1c68fa91","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:38.268Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `E.showError(title, e)`: show an error in the red box at the top of the page (the engine does it for errors in update and draw); a click hides it. Before play has started it shows on the boot screen instead, as a report a player can screenshot\n\n## 10b. Standard features\n\n- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n- `fullscreen.enter(quiet)`: go full screen. Browsers allow it only from a tap, click or key press: call it from one (a button, the menu, a key's update step). Returns a promise of whether it worked (a refusal is kept in failed and noted on screen, unless quiet)\n- `fullscreen.exit()`: leave full screen (Escape and the phone's back gesture do it too)\n- `fullscreen.on`: true while the page is full screen\n- `fullscreen.standalone`: true when the page was opened from a home screen as an app (no browser bars: nothing to go full screen from)\n- `fullscreen.supported`: true where this page can go full screen (not an iPhone, which has Add to Home Screen instead; not a frame without permission; not headless)\n- `fullscreen.toggle()`: full screen on or off, as the player asked (the corner's button, the menu): their choice is kept in settings.fullscreen, so a game starting on a phone goes full screen by itself only while they haven't turned it off\n- `fullscreen.failed = null`: game: the game it serves; failed: why the last request was refused (a message), or null\n\n## 10c. Boot\n\n789:    /** glyphs: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' |\n792:    this.glyphs = 'auto'; this.rumbleScale = .6; this.padLost = false;\n895:   *  button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family) */\n904:  /** the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says */\n906:    if (this.glyphs && this.glyphs !== 'auto') return this.glyphs;\n1302: * 6. PIXEL FONT  3x5 glyphs for in-world numbers and labels\n1354:  normal: { glyphs: parseFont(G57), h: 7, desc: 2, gap: 1, space: 3, upper: false },\n1355:  tiny: { glyphs: parseFont(GLYPHS), h: 5, desc: 0, gap: 2, space: 3, upper: true, mono: 3 }\n1369:  _glyph(f, ch) { return f.glyphs[f.upper ? ch.toUpperCase() : ch] || f.glyphs[ch.toUpperCase()] || f.glyphs['?']; },\n1426:   * Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge.\n2999:  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { g.input.glyphs = v; } },\n9107: *    changes